{}},{"entry":"main","kind":"reject","input":"40.1234-075.5678","expect":{}},{"entry":"main","kind":"reject","input":"+401234-075.5678","expect":{}}],"docs":{"lat":"±DD.DDDD — degrees latitude.","lon":"±DDD.DDDD — degrees longitude.","crs":"/Wnnn — the world-geodetic code suffix."},"source":"## ISO 6709 coordinates, the decimal-degree profile: a latitude\n## (±DD.DDDD) and longitude (±DDD.DDDD), optional altitude and the\n## terminating slash. Demonstrates fixed-count repetition and signed\n## fields.\ngrammar Iso6709 version \"1.0.0\" {\n  sign = %x2B / %x2D\n  digit = %x30-39\n  ## ±DD.DDDD — degrees latitude.\n  lat = sign 2digit \".\" 1*4digit as latitude\n  ## ±DDD.DDDD — degrees longitude.\n  lon = sign 3digit \".\" 1*4digit as longitude\n  altitude = sign 1*5digit \".\" 1*2digit as height\n  ## /Wnnn — the world-geodetic code suffix.\n  crs = \"/\" %x57 1*3digit\n  point = lat lon [ altitude ] [ crs ] [ \"/\" ]\n\n  entry main: point\n\n  test {\n    accept \"+40.1234-075.5678\"\n    accept \"+27.4716-070.1234/\"\n    accept \"-33.8688+151.2093+000.00/\"\n    reject \"40.1234-075.5678\"\n    reject \"+401234-075.5678\"\n  }\n}\n","source_hash":"b747bcbafa0a243b0e24ba6a3b42ac50584690b3133cfb20371cf4a709863dc3","compiler_version":"1.3.109","checksum":"sha256:91607af6451e0206d714e45d86d008597d146c17932fb5d555a49aa25399cce9"}
